            <ArticleTitle>Analgesic effect of olipiphate on mouse model of chemical stimulation of peritoneum.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>254-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We studied the analgesic effect of olipiphate, a product of lignin, against writhing provoked by intraperitoneal injection of acetic acid. Paracetamol was used as the reference drug. Both agents dose-dependently decreased the number of motor reactions caused by the irritant. Olipiphate possessed analgesic activity and efficiency comparable with those of paracetamol, but produced a more long-lasting effect.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
